{
    "//": [
        "The Plasma splash screen — plan/17. A Look-and-Feel package carrying ONE thing, the",
        "splash, because that is the unit Plasma's splash is packaged in: ksplashqml resolves",
        "ksplashrc's [KSplash] Theme as a Plasma/LookAndFeel package id and loads",
        "contents/splash/Splash.qml out of it (splashwindow.cpp, SplashWindow::setGeometry).",
        "",
        "It ships on every profile with a desktop, and /etc/xdg/ksplashrc names it for every",
        "user — see ../ksplashrc.in for why that one file covers the live account and every",
        "account Calamares creates.",
        "",
        "Everything this package does not ship still resolves to Breeze: plasma-workspace makes",
        "org.kde.breeze.desktop the FALLBACK package for any id but its own, so colours, style,",
        "lock screen, logout and the desktop layout are untouched. That is also why applying",
        "this as a Global Theme in System Settings is harmless rather than a way to end up with",
        "half a desktop.",
        "",
        "It is a SEPARATE package from @DISTRO_ID@-installer, which carries the live medium's",
        "task-manager layout script. Two packages because they have different lifetimes: this",
        "one ships in the product and the installed system, that one exists for twenty minutes",
        "on a USB stick. ksplashrc's Theme wins over kdeglobals' LookAndFeelPackage in",
        "ksplashqml's own resolution order, so the live session gets both."
    ],
    "KPackageStructure": "Plasma/LookAndFeel",
    "KPlugin": {
        "Id": "@DISTRO_ID@",
        "Name": "@DISTRO_NAME@",
        "Description": "The @DISTRO_NAME@ splash screen",
        "Category": "",
        "License": "GPL-2.0-or-later",
        "Authors": [
            {
                "Name": "@DISTRO_NAME@"
            }
        ],
        "Website": "@HOME_URL@"
    },
    "X-Plasma-APIVersion": "2"
}
